    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `contactPreference` rule: it returns `EMAIL` when an owner has an email, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing pattern used for computed fields like `membershipLevel` and `locality`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `contactPreference` property (readOnly string, enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field and a `ContactPreferenceEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto` plus a `contactPreference(owner)` default method that returns `EMAIL` when `owner.getEmail()` is present and non-empty, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite are green.",
